Mutations against scripts/avatar/springsim.parts.test.ts, 2026-09-11.

Each mutation is applied to scripts/avatar/springsim.ts alone, four suites are
run (parts, derive, springsim, grid), and the file is restored by writing back
the bytes read before the first mutation. Never `git checkout --`: the byte
comparison is asserted after every restore and again at the end.
node_modules/.vite is removed before every run. A mutation whose pattern does not
hit exactly once aborts rather than reporting green.

The names under each are the tests that failed. Six mutations, six red.

P1 gather reads each primitive's whole accessor again, the pre-fix behaviour
  RED: 1 failing suites
    - reads a shared vertex buffer once, not once per primitive
    - leaves out buffer vertices no triangle references
P2 the spring share is taken over the whole buffer again
  RED: 1 failing suites
    - splits one shared buffer between moving hair and everything else
P3 drawnVertices ignores the index list and claims the whole buffer
  RED: 1 failing suites
    - splits one shared buffer between moving hair and everything else
    - leaves out buffer vertices no triangle references
P4 a non-indexed primitive is treated as drawing nothing
  RED: 1 failing suites
    - counts every vertex of a primitive that carries no index list
P5 groups keyed by primitive rather than by buffer, so a shared buffer stacks again
  RED: 4 failing suites
    - reads a shared vertex buffer once, not once per primitive
    - leaves out buffer vertices no triangle references
    - is unchanged on a body whose primitives each own their buffer
    - produces the same set twice, so a re-measured file can be diffed
    - simulates a body with no manifest beside it, and gets a crown out of it
    - agrees on every query, on the face the penetration test is asked about
    - agrees on the body shell too, whose vertices are spread over a whole figure
    - finds a vertex that sits outside its own bounding box by less than REACH
    - saturates rather than reaching, for a point outside the geometry entirely
P6 a hair mesh may take the canonical Body_Skin name again
P6 a hair mesh may take the canonical Body_Skin name again (retry, after adding its test)
  RED: 1 failing suites
    - never lets a hair mesh be the body the penetration test measures against

Two of the six needed the tests tightened before they turned red, and both are
recorded here rather than quietly fixed, because a mutation that stays green is
the only signal that a defence has no test.

P2 stayed green on its first run. The test asserting the per-primitive share
used AvatarSample_B, whose mesh-wide average is ABOVE SPRING_DOMINATED, so
reverting to a mesh-wide reading still classified the whole mesh as hair and the
assertion (that some part is named Body_Skin) was satisfied by the body mesh
regardless. The discriminating fact on that body is that the hair mesh must
SPLIT between two roles; the test now pins that its Hair part and its trailing
Body_Skin part account for all 77 primitives between them.

P6 stayed green on its first run because the canonical-Body_Skin rule had no
test at all, which is what let the defect it fixes reach mika-pink's committed
clearance in the first place. The test added for it asserts that no mesh
supplying a Hair part is the one named Body_Skin, and separately that the
fixture actually poses the problem, so a rule that ignored the question could
not pass it.

BASELINE: 0 failing suites of 4
restored: springsim.ts byte-identical to the version read at start
